    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1896-98/document/27> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420766113/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """reading. Bernhard suggested music, and we concocted the following telegram to Placci – “ Secret of music enjoyment discovered! Eat sweets while listening .”
I continued my enraging search for paper and Bernhard finished his introduction to the “Central Italians”, which I read when I got back. I thought it very,  very  good. It is about visual images and their influence on so-called taste. 
Mr. Blaydes came to spend the evening with him, and I practised. I have laughed all day over the “great discovery!”
Sunday Nov. 15. 1896.
It rained, as it has done  almost every day  since the middle of August, and we spent our time working and reading. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 27 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1896-98> .

